# ── tests/ IS NOT EXCLUDED, deliberately ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# It was, and `Dockerfile.sentinel-test` — whose entire purpose is to run the
# suite INSIDE the certified image — then failed at `COPY tests/ /work/tests/`
# with "file not found in build context". A .dockerignore applies to the whole
# CONTEXT, so excluding a directory hides it from every Dockerfile built from
# this root, including the one that must have it.
#
# Leaving it in the context does NOT put it in any service image: no Dockerfile
# here does a broad `COPY . .` — every one names explicit paths — so tests/
# reaches only the image that asks for it by name. The cost is ~10MB of context,
# and `tests/sentinel/test_image_layout.py` asserts that every path any
# Dockerfile COPYs survives this file, so the next exclusion that breaks a build
# fails in CI rather than forty packages into an apt-get on the NAS.
